  "adaptations": {
    "contacts": "Adapted to starter app accounts and platform module doors; no SDK or organisation-account block. Source hashes identify the copied registry files before adaptation. Migration renamed to 0101-contacts.sql; storage transaction supplies organisation scope, revision checks, size limits and a row lock. Version 0.1.0 is the kit source snapshot label; the OSS registry has no version field.",
    "pipeline": "Adapted to starter app accounts and platform module doors; no SDK or organisation-account block. Source hashes identify the copied registry files before adaptation. Migration renamed to 0102-pipeline.sql; tasks use the same board with task labels. Version 0.1.0 is the kit source snapshot label; the OSS registry has no version field.",
    "password-reset": "Adapted to starter app accounts and platform module doors; no SDK or organisation-account block. Source hashes identify the copied registry files before adaptation. Registry sender/store replaced with starter reset-request and reset actions; migration is a compatibility marker because starter owns password proofs. Signed-in member change is not shipped. Version 0.1.0 is the kit source snapshot label; the OSS registry has no version field. Password crypto helpers extracted to lib/password.ts, retaining both formats and the four-derive cap. Sign-in atomically compares the old hash and invalidates sessions before creating a new session; CRM also invalidates reset proofs.",
    "theme": "Adapted to starter app accounts and platform module doors; no SDK or organisation-account block. Source hashes identify the copied registry files before adaptation. Remote font imports replaced by bundled font packages; global labels and buttons styled for clear, readable forms. Version 0.1.0 is the kit source snapshot label; the OSS registry has no version field.",
    "roles": "Organisation-scoped membership and records replace global account listing and owner-only personal records; one shared database pool. Only lib/roles/http.ts and the /api/roles and /owner/roles aliases are kept; the unscoped role guard, page guard, members and no-access files were removed because workspace access is checked in lib/pramaan/crm-data.ts.",
    "admin-table": "Organisation-scoped membership and records replace global account listing and owner-only personal records; one shared database pool."
  }
